That last difference is the reason for the schema bump rather than silently reinterpreting version 2. Stable imported AssetIds, MotionSlotIds, RetargetMap assets, HumanoidProfiles, and concrete ADR 0099 target clip identities remain unchanged. Motion-only import settings gain the optional `motion_humanoid_source_model` provenance described above so import can own one deterministic portable Humanoid candidate instead of deferring its creation to Animation Set resolution. Because the field is optional current behavior, a motion source without it remains valid and simply exposes no Humanoid candidate until a usable source is configured and reimported.

This ADR amends ADR 0110 as follows when accepted:

- Decision 3 is clarified so the portable Humanoid variant is import/reimport-owned and exists before Animation Set resolution; motion-only formats use stable canonical model provenance to build it;
- Decision 5 keeps lossless-first precedence for model-bound candidates but removes the explicit Native-only exception;
- Decision 6 is replaced by the logical-motion candidate list plus target-result presentation defined here; and
- Decision 7 stores the selected stable candidate rather than a three-way adaptation-policy tag.
